>>
Rule 1 (input must be a Tensor)
{input: tensor} |= ndim(input) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (input dtype must not be complex to avoid unsupported ComplexDouble)
{input: tensor} |= dtype_(input) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(input) ≠ 10
>>
Rule 3 (input should be a real floating tensor)
{input: tensor} |= 6 ≤ dtype_(input) ∧ dtype_(input) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 4 (out, if provided, must have the same shape as input)
{input: tensor, out: tensor} |= ndim(out) = ndim(input) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(input) - 1] : shape(out, i) = shape(input, i)
>>
Rule 5 (out, if provided, must be real floating and match input dtype)
{input: tensor, out: tensor} |= (6 ≤ dtype_(input) ∧ dtype_(input) ≤ 8) ∧ dtype_(out) = dtype_(input)
